-17 14:09:58 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-17 21:09:58 +07 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\n\nWrote `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md`. No other file was touched.\n\n**The brief's central premise was wrong, and it changes the plan.** The map↔rows codec already exists at `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:590-826`, committed as `84f8eef` on 2026-09-16 after a five-round review. Fifteen deftests cover it, and `semantic-bytecode-round-trip-law` in `test/yin/vm_test.cljc` already asserts both directions over a 29-program corpus of every tag. Item 13 is done, not \"testable now\". What the survey missed is that the code lives in `yin.vm` under the name the design gave it. The other two claims held: no expander, and the linearizer serves only the datom path. Nothing in `src/` consumes the codec yet.\n\n**Phases: Phase 0 plus three phases, sixteen units, six owner decisions.**\n\n- **Phase 0**: status-note corrections to the design (item 13 done, one open question missing from §10, a §7.1 vs §6.1 topology ambiguity).\n- **Phase 1, seven units, buildable now**: walker `:stream/close` arm, the full §7.4 row validator plus malformed corpus, walker row loader, lowering over rows to the canonical positional vector, §7.5 vector validator and positional loader with the projection-path equality tests, segment rows and syntactic extraction queries with the footprint table, and the occurrence relation with root-scoped rules. About three weeks.\n- **Phase 2, four units, mechanical after a decision**: profile publication and the semantic.md amendment (item 14), derivation records and ledger, rows in `dao.jing`, the observer row lane.\n- **Phase 3, five units, genuinely speculative**: UCF amendments, primitive profiles, work-item dependency closure, occurrence identity end to end, the expander and batch protocol. Two to three months against documents that are themselves unimplemented proposals.\n\n**Ready to build vs blocked.** Items 2, 6 (syntactic half), 5 (extraction half), and the never-listed §3.2/§7.4/§7.5 work are ready. Items 7, 9, 10, 14 wait on an owner approval or choice. Items 3, 4, 5, 8, 11 are owed to UCF, `yin.vm.macro.md`, or a ruling on the batch coordinate. Two findings the design does not carry: UCF is untracked in git, so item 8 has nothing to amend yet, and no portable batch coordinate exists anywhere because v2 cursors are positionless and the macro expander's counter is process-local.\n\n**Recommendation, one line:** start Phase 1 today with the §7.4 validator and the close arm, put the profile-publication and walker-medium decisions in front of the owner now so Phase 2 follows without a gap, and do not open Phase 3 until UCF is committed.","ttft_ms":75077,"type":"result","duration_ms":348563,"uuid":"f0b87eed-2158-4c0a-b642-75b5bfb6d2cf","ttft_stream_ms":2987,"time_to_request_ms":22,"first_content_frame_ms":2987,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":1}
